# Fetch

`fetch` is the native system-and-CPU command from
[`keys-i/tools`](https://github.com/keys-i/tools). It reports host, operating
system, kernel, architecture, CPU, topology, caches, core counts, memory,
shell, and terminal without starting Python or a shell subprocess.

The dashboard exposes the stable `format` choices `--plain` and `--json`.
Running `fetch` directly in a terminal uses the styled view. `NO_COLOR=1`
disables decoration.

Build [`keys-i/tools`](https://github.com/keys-i/tools) and place `fetch` on
`PATH`. The prepared `keys-tools` PyPI package has not been published. This
script pack does not download or install binaries.
